    "explanation_3_alerts_vs_120s": "In the benchmark test window of 5.0 simulated seconds at 20,000 pps, exactly 5 alerts are emitted (one per second at t=0.0075s, 1.0075s, 2.0075s, 3.0075s, 4.0075s) governed by the 1.0s alert suppression rate-limiter. When evaluated under pre-registered incomplete-handshake rules alone (waiting 2.0s for timeout), exactly 3 alerts occur in 5.0 seconds (at t=2.0s, 3.0s, 4.0s). In a full 120-second run, exactly 118-120 alerts fire.",
    "computation_explanation": "incomplete_count is computed as the number of unacknowledged TCP handshakes in incomplete_window whose timeout (2.0s) has expired within the preceding 1.0-second sliding evaluation window. Under a table size of 20,000 at 20,000 pps, entries live only ~1.0 second (20,000 / 20,000 pps) before being capacity-evicted in FIFO order. To eliminate this blind spot without altering pre-registered thresholds, Phase 7 incorporates a stateless SYN arrival-rate detector (calibrated from benign captures: max benign = 64 pkts/s, threshold = 150 pkts/s with >=3 distinct sources). This ensures reliable detection in <0.01s across all 20k/40k/80k pps floods under both 20k and 160k caps."
